hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16309","He said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid and Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, he said: 'Urwah ibn Mudarris informed me, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Jam', and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from the two mountains of Tayyi, I have wearied myself and exhausted my mount, and by Allah, I have not left any mountain but I stood upon it, so is there Hajj for me? So he said: Whoever witnessed with us this prayer, meaning the Fajr prayer at Jam', and stood with us until we pour forth from it, and he had poured forth before that from 'Arafat by night or day, then his Hajj is complete and he has completed his rite."
"16310","He said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: 'Urwah ibn Mudarris ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam narrated to me, that he performed Hajj in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not reach the people except by night while he was at Jam', so he went to 'Arafat and poured forth from it, then returned and came to Jam', and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wearied myself and exhausted my mount, so is there Hajj for me? So he said: Whoever prayed with us the morning prayer at Jam' and stood with us until we pour forth, and he had poured forth before that from 'Arafat by night or day, then his Hajj is complete and he has completed his rite."
